      "message": "fix(post): state the stock's turning radius on lathe streams\n\nA lathe or mill-turn stream now carries PARAM StockTurnRadius: the\nlargest distance of a stock vertex from the spindle axis. The Tormach\nlathe post takes the larger of this radius and the box half-width for\nits G30 approach and departure, so the rotating corners of a square\nbar are clear. Mill streams do not change.\n\nThe goldens tormach-lathe/axial_drill_mm.nc and axial_drill_inch.nc\nare not regenerated here: their 24 x 24 box stock moves the final\ndeparture from X24 to X33.941 (corner diameter). The maintainer\ndecides on the golden change.\n\nRefs #1666\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
